  "id": "csango_moldavian_music",
  "name": "Csángó zene (Moldavian Csángó song and dance music)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Music of the Csángós, Roman Catholic Hungarian-speaking communities of Romanian Moldavia around Bacău and the Siret valley, whose village repertoire kept archaic layers of Hungarian song alongside dance tunes shared with their Romanian neighbours. Unaccompanied ballads, laments and religious songs sit beside dance music for furulya duct flute, koboz lute, violin and a small drum (dob); Zoltán Kallós and other collectors recorded it from the mid-twentieth century, and Hungarian dance-house (táncház) musicians later took up the repertoire. The membrane-drum card stands in for the dob.",
  "recipe": "classic modern csángó zene, field Work, Slavic balkan branch. solo unaccompanied. traditional furulya, archaic dry plucked koboz, fiddle, membrane drum pulse resonant acoustic membrane drum. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
